Output port 0: {"name": "Action", "type": "delimited", "fields": [{"name": "action", "type": "string", "nullable": "false"}]}

reference:
```ctl
//#CTL2
string[] actions;
function integer count() {
    if ($in.0.notify) append(actions, "NOTIFY");
    if ($in.0.archive) append(actions, "ARCHIVE");
    return length(actions);
}
function integer transform(integer idx) {
    $out.0.action = actions[idx];
    return ALL;
}
function void clean() { clear(actions); }
```

JavaScript let actions is undefined and needs an array assignment before push. The CTL2 list is empty on declaration; count can append immediately, and clean prevents the previous input’s actions from leaking into the next one.

